    "convention": "f(h) = W h + b is the vector WRITTEN into the recipient at L2_SINGLE; every ablation acts on that final affine output. Ablations are reported BOTH as zero-ablation and as mean-ablation against mu_native (the recipient's mean native L2_SINGLE state on the same problems). If they diverge, report the mean-ablation number.",
    "seed_convention": "every bare key is DETAIL_SEED = task_maps[0] with a Wilson interval over ITEMS (unchanged from the single-seed run). A key ending in '_acrossseed' is the mean over FOLLOWUP_SEEDS with an ACROSS-SEED t-interval, and the matching '_per_seed' key holds the raw values. The two intervals answer different questions \u2014 item noise vs map-training noise \u2014 so both are reported.",
    "single_seed_caveat": "DETAIL_SEED = task_maps[0] for the full sweep/curve/geometry keys (unchanged); the HEADLINE quantity of this experiment is ALSO reported over FOLLOWUP_SEEDS [0, 1, 2, 3, 4] in the '*_acrossseed' (across-seed t-interval) and '*_per_seed' keys. The 5-seed spread of the base channel is in RESULTS['arithmetic']['task_unsolv_full_per_seed'].",
    "multiseed_scope": "Multi-seeded HEADLINES only: A = MISMATCH three-way first-token split + MATCHED adapted rate; B = first_token_is_donor_answer_y_P and its excess over the (DETAIL_SEED) empirical null; C = unembedding_ablated_first ZERO and MEAN; D = proj_only_natural__first and comp_only_natural__first for the INLP-540 and UNEMB subspaces; E = svd_ablated zero/mean at j in [2, 16]. Everything else (SHUFFLED/NATIVE conditions, the INLP rank sweep, rank-360 and the rescaled/meanfill variants of D, the rest of E's curve, all random controls, all principal angles and containment) stays at DETAIL_SEED = 0."
